====================================================================================================
J1. SPARC dwarfs in the deep-MOND regime: residuals vs MOND alone, and what a cold halo would add
====================================================================================================
  27 dwarfs (M_b < 1e9 Msun, Q<=2, i>=30); deep-MOND points: g_bar < 0.1 a_0
  canonical : 26 dwarfs: per-galaxy mean residual = -0.105 +/- 0.049 (SE), galaxy-to-galaxy scatter 0.250 dex | AM halo would add +0.33 dex (median) | tolerance |mean| + 2 SE + 0.1 = 0.303 -> f_max = 0.87
  alt       : 27 dwarfs: per-galaxy mean residual = -0.143 +/- 0.046 (SE), galaxy-to-galaxy scatter 0.240 dex | AM halo would add +0.31 dex (median) | tolerance |mean| + 2 SE + 0.1 = 0.335 -> f_max = 1.10
  [PASS] J1a MOND alone fits the deep-MOND dwarfs on the sample MEAN: |per-galaxy mean residual| < 0.15 dex on at least one footing, and the dwarfs sit AT or BELOW the MOND line, not above it (no room for an additive halo)   (canonical: -0.105 +/- 0.049; alt: -0.143 +/- 0.046)
  [PASS] J1b a cold-component halo at the abundance-matched level would add > 0.30 dex to those points (median), i.e. MOND + cold double-counts the dwarfs by > 2x, both footings   (canonical: +0.33 dex; alt: +0.31 dex)
  [FAIL] J1c even with a 0.10 dex systematic floor on the sample mean, the dwarfs allow at most 60% of the abundance-matched halo (both footings)   (canonical: f_max = 0.87; alt: f_max = 1.10)

====================================================================================================
J2. removing the dwarfs' halos needs a cutoff the forest forbids
====================================================================================================
  M_hm >= 2.0e+10 Msun (the dwarfs' own halo mass (16th pct)) -> m_WDM <= 0.91 keV
  M_hm >= 2.0e+11 Msun (10x that, so their halos are truly absent, not just fewer/less concentrated) -> m_WDM <= 0.46 keV
  forest: m_WDM >= 3.5 keV (Viel+ 2013, loose) / 5.3 keV (Irsic+ 2017)  ->  M_hm <= 2.3e+08 / 5.7e+07 Msun
  [PASS] J2 the cutoff that would empty the dwarfs' halos (m_WDM <= ~0.3-0.5 keV) is excluded by the LOOSE forest bound (3.5 keV) by > 5x in mass, > 200x in half-mode mass: the cold component the forest needs must sit in the dwarfs   (m_need = 0.46 keV vs 3.5 keV: x8; M_hm ratio x874)

====================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  The framework's only self-consistent form after today is MOND plus a cold, ballistic, galaxy-clustering component.  In the
  deep-MOND dwarfs the data sit at or below MOND alone and tolerate well under the halo such a component would bring; removing
  that halo needs a free-streaming cutoff the forest excludes by more than an order of magnitude.  So the cold component the
  CMB, the Bullet and the forest require is in the dwarfs, and the dwarfs say it is not there on top of MOND.  The combination
  is excluded from inside the framework's own galaxies.  What that leaves is the dichotomy, now with numbers on both sides:
  either the RAR is the cold component (LCDM, no MOND) or the cold component is not there (MOND, no CMB/Bullet/forest).

RESULT: 4 checks, 1 FAIL -> ['J1c even with a 0.10 dex systematic floor on the sample mean, the dwarfs allow at most 60% of the abundance-matched halo (both footings)']   rc=1
